## 3. Functional Requirements

### 3.1 Movie Search
| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-1 | The system shall provide a text input field for entering a movie title. |
| FR-2 | The system shall query the TMDB API as the user types, using a debounce delay to limit request frequency. |
| FR-3 | The system shall display a list of matching movies with poster thumbnail, title, and release year. |
| FR-4 | The system shall display an appropriate message when no results are found. |

### 3.2 Movie Detail View
| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-5 | The system shall allow the user to select a movie from the results list to view full details. |
| FR-6 | The system shall display plot summary, cast, genre, runtime, release date, and rating for the selected movie. |
| FR-7 | The system shall allow the user to return to the search results from the detail view. |

### 3.3 Animation and Transitions
| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-8 | The system shall animate the appearance of search results (e.g., fade-in or staggered entry). |
| FR-9 | The system shall display an animated loading indicator while awaiting API responses. |
| FR-10 | The system shall animate the transition between the search view and the detail view. |
| FR-11 | The system shall apply hover/interaction animations to result cards. |

### 3.4 Error Handling
| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-12 | The system shall display a user-friendly error message if the TMDB API request fails. |
| FR-13 | The system shall handle empty or whitespace-only search input without triggering an API call. |

### 3.5 Responsive Design
| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-14 | The system shall render correctly on screen widths from mobile (≥320px) to desktop. |
| FR-15 | The system shall maintain animation performance across supported device sizes. |

