## 4. External Interface Requirements

### 4.1 User Interfaces
A single-page web interface consisting of a search bar, a results grid, and a detail view, connected by animated transitions.

### 4.2 Hardware Interfaces
None. The application runs entirely within a web browser on standard consumer hardware.

### 4.3 Software Interfaces
| Interface | Description |
|---|---|
| TMDB API | RESTful API used to fetch movie search results and details; requires an API key for authentication. |

### 4.4 Communication Interfaces
Standard HTTPS requests over the internet to TMDB's servers.

---

## 5. Non-Functional Requirements

| ID | Category | Requirement |
|---|---|---|
| NFR-1 | Performance | Search results shall load within 2 seconds under normal network conditions. |
| NFR-2 | Usability | The interface shall be navigable without instructions, using conventional search UI patterns. |
| NFR-3 | Reliability | The system shall recover gracefully from failed API calls without crashing. |
| NFR-4 | Security | The TMDB API key shall not be exposed in client-side source control (managed via environment variables). |
| NFR-5 | Maintainability | Code shall be organized into reusable, modular components to support future feature additions. |
| NFR-6 | Portability | The application shall function consistently across major modern browsers. |

